sentences.l:
Of these one having lifted, Helen carried, heavenly-one of women,
that which was fairest in its intricate work and largest,
and like a star it shone forth;

silver
it is entirely, and with gold upon its rims it has been finished,
the work of Hephaestus;

and gave it to me Phaedimus the hero,
king of the Sidonians, when his own house sheltered
me there, on my way home;

and he then the shining mixing-bowl
set down in front of him, bringing it, strong Megapenthes,
of silver;

“A gift for you I too give, dear child, this one,
a memorial of Helen's hands, for the hour of much-loved marriage,
for your wife to wear;

And hand-water a handmaid poured over them, bringing it in a pitcher,
a fine golden one, over a silver basin,
for washing;

So then, to him as he spoke, there flew up on the right a bird,
an eagle, carrying a white goose in its talons, a huge one,
tame, from the courtyard;
